@startuml
title Vapor Composition Model

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "Steam App" {
    component "Steam App Instance" as SteamInstance

    package "Selected Vapor Context" {
        component "Vapor App Composition" as Composition
        component "Vapor App" as VaporApp
    }
}

package "Vapor Source / Composition Model" {
    component "Packagepack" as Packagepack

    package "Reusable Pack Fragments" {
        component "Enginepack" as Enginepack
        component "Gamepack" as Gamepack
        component "Modpack" as Modpack
    }

    package "Behavioral Content" {
        component "Engine" as Engine
        component "Game" as Game
        component "Engine Mod(s)" as EngineMods
        component "Game Mod(s)" as GameMods
        component "Extension Mod(s)" as ExtensionMods
    }
}

Packagepack --> Enginepack : may reference
Packagepack --> Gamepack : may reference
Packagepack --> Modpack : may reference

Packagepack --> Engine : may reference directly
Packagepack --> Game : may reference directly
Packagepack --> EngineMods : may reference directly
Packagepack --> GameMods : may reference directly
Packagepack --> ExtensionMods : may reference directly

Enginepack --> Engine : exactly one
Enginepack --> EngineMods : zero or more

Gamepack --> Game : exactly one
Gamepack --> GameMods : zero or more

Modpack --> EngineMods
Modpack --> GameMods
Modpack --> ExtensionMods

ExtensionMods --> EngineMods : may extend
ExtensionMods --> GameMods : may extend
ExtensionMods --> ExtensionMods : may extend

Packagepack --> Composition : resolve
Composition --> VaporApp : build / deploy

SteamInstance --> Composition : selects
SteamInstance --> VaporApp : installs / launches

note right of Engine
The effective Engine
declares the composition's
main binary.
end note

note bottom of Packagepack
A valid Packagepack represents
one complete composition.
end note

note bottom of VaporApp
A Vapor App is a built,
target-specific realization
of the resolved composition.
end note

@enduml